<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- Owner 2026-10-18: the dev flavor talks to the Mac on the LAN over
         plain http (API, MinIO, tools/fake-bunny.mjs on :4010) in EVERY
         build type, not only debug. Dart's HttpClient ignores Android's
         cleartext policy, so a release or profile dev build loaded the
         feed and covers but the video player (ExoPlayer, native) refused
         http://…:4010/…/playlist.m3u8 and a reel never played on Android.
         staging/prod stay https-only (no cleartext there). Security
         research #5 (2026-10-22), B2: the allowance now lives in this
         flavor's res/xml/network_security_config.xml (the manifest flag is
         ignored once a network security config is set). -->
</manifest>
